WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.890
Mandalorian's great.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.723
Yes, it is.

00:00:02.723 --> 00:00:04.230
Mandalorian's awesome.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.910
No, if they, if they did the whole series

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.120
the way this thing looks like
a spaghetti Western in space,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.503
I would have been all over it.

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:11.523
Well, it's so funny, by the way,

00:00:11.523 --> 00:00:15.720
Because I liked, you
know, I like Blade Runner.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.430
Here's what's amazing, what you just said.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.400
So I was 12, my aunt and uncle were

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.700
what they used to call rotoscope artists.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.700
Rotoscoping was the original
special effects by hand.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.150
They would have to paint,
hand paint individual frames

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:39.587
of movies to do things,
and they told me, I said,

00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:40.420
"What are you working on?"

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.510
Because I wanted to be in the movies.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.105
I was 12 years old

00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:48.105
and they go, "We're doing
this like really dumb movie."

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:52.380
"It's basically like a
spaghetti Western in space."

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.470
"It's called 'Star Wars,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.040
and we're drawing in the laser beams."

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.970
So literally the people who first worked

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.230
on the original "Star Wars" thought

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.140
it was a spaghetti Western in space.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:04.973
Wow.

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:06.250
And that's what you're,
what you're picking up on,

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.230
on Mandalorian.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.500
Clearly Favreau, you know, knew that,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.110
and that's why he's so great,
as a director, Jon Favreau.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.770
Yeah, and they're like such
huge, ridiculous fans of it.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.230
So I think it works for me
not knowing a lot about it.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.270
So then the weight of it,

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.634
which I didn't understand
until the first season came out

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.480
and then like this whole new
group of people were coming up

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.830
to me, super polite, "Star Wars" fans.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.663
At least when they meet you.

00:01:35.663 --> 00:01:36.700
I don't know how they are on the internet.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.490
I haven't read anything, but
like, they come up very polite

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.930
and like ridiculously passionate about,

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.276
it's like sports passion for a show, so.

00:01:47.276 --> 00:01:48.130
For sure.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.930
I've gotten, it's been real
cool that they came, you know,

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.070
it's funny, I get shit, though.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.740
They go, "I never heard a Boston accent

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.360
in a galaxy far, far away."

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.270
And I always go like,
"Well, how about English?"

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.103
"You don't think it's weird

00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:02.385
that they're all speaking English?"

00:02:02.385 --> 00:02:03.218
(laughs)

00:02:03.218 --> 00:02:04.760
What was, what was the question?

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:05.810
The whole thing's ridiculous.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:06.643
Exactly.

00:02:06.643 --> 00:02:07.583
There's a Sasquatch.

00:02:08.455 --> 00:02:09.440
(attempts Wookiee roar) Yeah.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.920
Yeah.
The Wookiee.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.930
And what I love is Han Solo
still speaks in English to him

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.350
and they both understand each other

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.670
but he doesn't grunt like him

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.050
and he doesn't speak in
English to him, but it works.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.330
You can't, you can't start
using that kind of logic

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.163
in "Star Wars"

00:02:23.163 --> 00:02:25.480
or the whole thing falls
apart pretty quickly.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.514
Exactly. Then they should
leave my Boston accent alone.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.597
(laughs)

